\contentsline {table}{\numberline {4.1}{\ignorespaces Syntactic contrast accuracy and perplexity (PPL) for baseline and kNN-LM models ($k=16$, $\tau =3$, sequence-level retrieval). kNN augmentation improves accuracy across all phenomena and both pretraining scales, with relative clauses showing the largest gains. Perplexity reductions are larger for the large-scale model. Bold indicates improvement over baseline.}}{51}{table.caption.52}%
